{"title":"Multinomial Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Multinomial Theorem</b> states that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cb6228eda6d98ac694f0fa5bf19c95eb0edff4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_k)^n=\\sum_{\\substack{j_1,j_2,\\ldots,j_k \\\\ 0 \\leq j_i \\leq n \\textrm{ for each } i \\\\ \\textrm{and } j_1 + \\ldots + j_k = n}}\\binom{n}{j_1; j_2; \\ldots ; j_k}a_1^{j_1}a_2^{j_2}\\cdots a_k^{j_k}\\]\" width=\"485\" height=\"78\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fcb72e465c0f2e5d63ff75c0083a070dafbe6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{j_1; j_2; \\ldots ; j_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"118\" height=\"53\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_coefficient&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Multinomial coefficient (page does not exist)\">multinomial coefficient</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed82fb85648b03a21e5257533774d3528ba3870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{j_1; j_2; \\ldots ; j_k}=\\dfrac{n!}{j_1!\\cdot j_2!\\cdots j_k!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"250\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Note that this is a direct generalization of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_Theorem\" title=\"Binomial Theorem\">Binomial Theorem</a>, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e44ca2cae6be42148fe1b1fd8b5d55bd6b599bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> it simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5dc64793d2f619276e8443c44d83a30551fdd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1 + a_2)^n = \\sum_{\\substack{0\\leq j_1, j_2 \\leq n \\\\ j_1 + j_2 = n}} \\binom{n}{j_1; j_2} a_1^{j_1}a_2^{j_2} = \\sum_{j = 0}^n \\binom{n}{j} a_1^j a_2^{n - j}\\]\" width=\"422\" height=\"66\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_by_Induction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof by Induction</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_by_Combination\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof by Combination</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_by_Induction\">Proof by Induction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof by Induction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Proving the Multinomial Theorem by Induction\n</p><p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and a non-negative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d11a74278ed5eab745d54eeccfdfddf6ea769a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + ... + x_{k-1} + x_k)^n = \\sum_{b_1 + b_2 + b_3 + ... + b_{k-1} + b_k= n}{\\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ..., b_{k-1}, b_k} \\prod_{j=1}^{k}{x_j^{b_j}}}\\]\" width=\"630\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/25387657d7f99a4365b47c7775c5016b27d49623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bf Proof:$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\nWhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> the result is true, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> the result is the binomial theorem. Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bb76208dae30e44513fa10ff49ba1329094713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and that the result is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f465cb60a948a589f634bd0e337cd624328367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/771abfacf3f0d119f01b75de06bc9b5f9b1badb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d648620465c99f7dd021ec43e8ed00b6d29cda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + ... + x_{p-1} + x_p)^n = (x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + ... + x_{p-1} + (x_p +x_{p+1})^n\\]\" width=\"509\" height=\"18\" />\nTreating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751aa04a38cd870d4beb2b2a40b8d548b4b46857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_p + x_{p+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> as a single term and using the induction hypothesis:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c8a415551a33079071c985d94a5669fdf0107e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{b_1 + b_2 + b_3 + ... + b_{p-1} + B = n}{\\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ..., b_{p-1}, B} \\cdot (x_p + x_{p+1})^B \\cdot \\prod_{j=1}^{p-1}{x_j^{b_j}}}\\]\" width=\"510\" height=\"55\" />\nBy the Binomial Theorem, this becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c434ee9b7813596e960707c674c7ad067e814cab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{b_1 + b_2 + b_3 + ... + b_{p-1} + B = n}{\\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ..., b_{p-1}, B}} (\\prod_{j=1}^{p-1}{x_j^{b_j}}) \\cdot \\sum_{b_p + b_{p+1} = B}{\\binom{B}{b_p} \\cdot x_p^{b_p} x_{p+1}^{b_{p+1}}}\\]\" width=\"595\" height=\"55\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bdf0ee07875c57c8e0e0eb94bebdd7540eb081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ... ,b_p, B}\\binom{B}{b_p} = \\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ... ,b_p, b_{p+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"400\" height=\"53\" />, this can be rewritten as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0db0d000306d504aa7c78063fc84dd17f691893.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{b_1 + b_2 + ...  b_p + b_{p+1}= n}{\\binom{n}{b_1, b_2, b_3, ..., b_p, b_{p+1}}\\prod_{j=1}^{k}{x_j^{b_j}}}\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_by_Combination\">Proof by Combination</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof by Combination\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the multinomial expression\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f6a0a597e3273bc03fa0ace41854f26b2db421.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_m)^n.\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This can be written as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4e775209b3add230af96e7cdbabe5e765eb11c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\underbrace{(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_m)(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_m)\\cdots(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_m)}_{n\\text{ factors}}.\\]\" width=\"509\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>To obtain the term\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97447e552997359914ec8da3e7567a672ca8e7de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1^{k_1}a_2^{k_2}\\cdots a_m^{k_m},\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>we must choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> of the factors, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> of the factors, and so on, where\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffcabebec48c553c591de8a7669fa6fdf2ca5f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k_1+k_2+\\cdots+k_m=n.\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The number of ways to make these choices is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0221b5c5a7760c1ae0fe9b1ca95724b566179c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n!}{k_1!k_2!\\cdots k_m!}.\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the coefficient of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f900c594b258a179719a64d8e53cb27227d75ec1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1^{k_1}a_2^{k_2}\\cdots a_m^{k_m}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0221b5c5a7760c1ae0fe9b1ca95724b566179c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n!}{k_1!k_2!\\cdots k_m!}.\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/27005f48d0f8b3e6abc74ec558718dccb4688c8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_m)^n = \\sum_{\\substack{k_1+k_2+\\cdots+k_m=n\\\\k_1,k_2,\\ldots,k_m\\geq 0}} \\frac{n!}{k_1!k_2!\\cdots k_m!} a_1^{k_1}a_2^{k_2}\\cdots a_m^{k_m}.\\]\" width=\"509\" height=\"60\" />\n</p><p>This proves the multinomial theorem combinatorially.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expression</a></li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967fd0b1012b67df0bed030293f8a3ce757aaf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y+z)^{2006}+(x-y-z)^{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />\nis simplified by expanding it and combining like terms. How many terms are in the simplified expression?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc589a8190f0c7ffe0cf241b00b8f4a0f4c90a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ }6018\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)\\ }671,676\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)\\ }1,007,514\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)\\ }1,008,016\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)\\ }2,015,028$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"637\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>(Source: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">2006 AMC 12A Problem 24</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multinomial_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234742\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 192/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7390/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3294:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234742 and revision id 286447. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}